Q: How can I validate menu input (1–4) and prevent my C program from terminating on invalid character input? A: <ol>
<li>Determine what would be a reasonable large buffer to accept a <em>line</em> of input.   Be generous, yet not insane</li>
</ol>
<pre><code>#define LINE_N 80
char buf[LINE_N];
</code></pre>
<ol start="2">
<li>Use <code>fgets()</code> to read  the <em>line</em><sup>*1</sup>  of input into a <em>string</em><sup>*2</sup>.  Test for success of reading input - any input by testing <code>fgets()</code> return value.  Do <em>not</em> continue reading on end-of-file.<br />
TBD: how to handle rare input error.</li>
</ol>
<pre><code>while (fgets(buf, sizeof buf, stdin)) {
  ...
}
</code></pre>
<ol start="3">
<li>Test the string.  In this case, test for a numeric value and if in range.</li>
</ol>
<pre><code>  int value_min = 1;
  int value_max = 4;
  char *end;
  errno = 0;
  long value = strtol(buf, &amp;end, 10);
  // Successful conversion string to an integer?
  // Did conversion stop on a '\n'?
  // In range?
  if (end != buf &amp;&amp; *end == `'\n'` &amp;&amp; value &gt;= value_min &amp;&amp; value &lt;= value_max) {
    break;
  }
}
</code></pre>
<ol start="4">
<li>Consider packaging this as a function</li>
</ol>
<pre><code>// Return success flag.
int read_int(int *val, int value_min, value_max) {
  ...
}
</code></pre>
<hr />
<p>*Advanced issues:</p>
<ol>
<li>Handling excessively long lines.</li>
<li>Allowing or non-white-space before and/or after the numeric text.</li>
<li>Allowing non-based 10 input.</li>
<li>Handling rare input error.</li>
<li>Type concerns.</li>
</ol>
<hr />
<p><sup>*1</sup><br />
A text stream is an ordered sequence of characters composed into <em>lines</em>, each <em>line</em> consisting of zero or more characters plus a terminating new-line character. Whether the last line requires a terminating new-line character is implementation-defined.</p>
<p><sup>*2</sup><br />
A <em>string</em> is a contiguous sequence of characters terminated by and including the first null character.</p>

Q: Displaying nested objects in XAML A: <p>I'm writing a quick response. It's temporary. I'll edit it this evening or tomorrow. The purpose of this quick response is to avoid making the author of the question wait too long for their question to be resolved. It also allows the author of the question to clarify the requirements for the final version.</p>
<p>Link to the repository with all files: <a href="https://gist.github.com/EldHasp/ad5b3c5ea8d72490e3d3f4c998a5d2b4" rel="nofollow noreferrer">https://gist.github.com/EldHasp/ad5b3c5ea8d72490e3d3f4c998a5d2b4</a></p>
<p>XAML of the main element (UserControl):</p>
<pre class="lang-xml prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;UserControl x:Class=&quot;SOQuestions2025.Questions.user32602103.question79981370.WeekDaysGrid&quot;
             xmlns=&quot;http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation&quot;
             xmlns:x=&quot;http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml&quot;
             xmlns:d=&quot;http://schemas.microsoft.com/expression/blend/2008&quot;
             xmlns:mc=&quot;http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/markup-compatibility/2006&quot;
             xmlns:local=&quot;clr-namespace:SOQuestions2025.Questions.user32602103.question79981370&quot;
             mc:Ignorable=&quot;d&quot;
             d:DesignHeight=&quot;300&quot; d:DesignWidth=&quot;600&quot;
             d:DataContext=&quot;{d:DesignInstance Type=local:Week, IsDesignTimeCreatable=False}&quot;&gt;
    &lt;UserControl.Resources&gt;
        &lt;DataTemplate x:Key=&quot;{x:Static local:ItineraryColumns.NestRowTemplateKey}&quot;
                      DataType=&quot;{x:Type local:NestRow}&quot;&gt;
            &lt;UniformGrid Columns=&quot;3&quot;&gt;
                &lt;Border BorderBrush=&quot;Gray&quot; BorderThickness=&quot;0.5&quot; Padding=&quot;4,2&quot;&gt;
                    &lt;TextBlock Text=&quot;{Binding NestNumber}&quot; TextAlignment=&quot;Center&quot;/&gt;
                &lt;/Border&gt;
                &lt;Border BorderBrush=&quot;Gray&quot; BorderThickness=&quot;0.5&quot; Padding=&quot;4,2&quot;&gt;
                    &lt;TextBlock Text=&quot;{Binding OrdersComplete}&quot; TextAlignment=&quot;Center&quot;/&gt;
                &lt;/Border&gt;
                &lt;Border BorderBrush=&quot;Gray&quot; BorderThickness=&quot;0.5&quot; Padding=&quot;4,2&quot;&gt;
                    &lt;TextBlock Text=&quot;{Binding OrdersTotal}&quot; TextAlignment=&quot;Center&quot;/&gt;
                &lt;/Border&gt;
            &lt;/UniformGrid&gt;
        &lt;/DataTemplate&gt;
    &lt;/UserControl.Resources&gt;

    &lt;DataGrid x:Name=&quot;daysGrid&quot;
              AutoGenerateColumns=&quot;True&quot;
              CanUserAddRows=&quot;False&quot;
              CanUserReorderColumns=&quot;False&quot;
              CanUserSortColumns=&quot;False&quot;
              IsReadOnly=&quot;True&quot;
              HeadersVisibility=&quot;Column&quot;/&gt;
&lt;/UserControl&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>Code Behinde:</p>
<pre class="lang-cs prettyprint-override"><code>using System.Windows;
using System.Windows.Controls;

namespace SOQuestions2025.Questions.user32602103.question79981370
{
    public partial class WeekDaysGrid : UserControl
    {
        public WeekDaysGrid()
        {
            InitializeComponent();
            daysGrid.AutoGeneratedColumns += ItineraryColumns.OnAutoGeneratedColumns;
        }

        public Week? Week
        {
            get =&gt; (Week?)GetValue(WeekProperty);
            set =&gt; SetValue(WeekProperty, value);
        }

        public static readonly DependencyProperty WeekProperty =
            DependencyProperty.Register(
                nameof(Week),
                typeof(Week),
                typeof(WeekDaysGrid),
                new PropertyMetadata(null, OnWeekChanged));

        private static void OnWeekChanged(DependencyObject d, DependencyPropertyChangedEventArgs e)
        {
            WeekDaysGrid control = (WeekDaysGrid)d;
            Week? week = e.NewValue as Week;

            control.daysGrid.Tag = week;
            control.daysGrid.ItemsSource = week?.Days;

            ItineraryColumns.GenerateMachineColumns(control.daysGrid, week);
        }
    }
}
</code></pre>
<p>Helper ItineraryColumns.cs:</p>
<pre class="lang-cs prettyprint-override"><code>    public static class ItineraryColumns
    {
        public const string NestRowTemplateKey = &quot;NestRowTemplate&quot;;

        /// &lt;summary&gt;
        /// After DataGrid finishes auto-generating columns for &lt;see cref=&quot;Day&quot;/&gt;,
        /// replace them with Day + one template column per machine of the selected week.
        /// DataGrid.Tag must be the selected &lt;see cref=&quot;Week&quot;/&gt;.
        /// &lt;/summary&gt;
        public static EventHandler OnAutoGeneratedColumns { get; } = (object? sender, EventArgs e) =&gt;
        {
            if (sender is not DataGrid dataGrid)
                return;

            GenerateMachineColumns(dataGrid, dataGrid.Tag as Week);
        };

        public static void GenerateMachineColumns(DataGrid dataGrid, Week? week)
        {
            dataGrid.Columns.Clear();
            if (week is null)
                return;

            dataGrid.Columns.Add(new DataGridTextColumn
            {
                Header = &quot;Day&quot;,
                Binding = new Binding(nameof(Day.Date)) { StringFormat = &quot;ddd, dd.MM&quot; },
                Width = new DataGridLength(1, DataGridLengthUnitType.Auto),
            });

            DataTemplate nestRowTemplate =
                dataGrid.TryFindResource(NestRowTemplateKey) as DataTemplate
                ?? CreateNestRowTemplate();

            for (int i = 0; i &lt; week.MachineNames.Count; i++)
            {
                FrameworkElementFactory itemsControl = new(typeof(ItemsControl));
                itemsControl.SetBinding(ItemsControl.ItemsSourceProperty, new Binding($&quot;Machines[{i}].Nests&quot;));
                itemsControl.SetValue(ItemsControl.ItemTemplateProperty, nestRowTemplate);

                FrameworkElementFactory outer = new(typeof(Border));
                outer.SetValue(Border.BorderBrushProperty, System.Windows.Media.Brushes.Gray);
                outer.SetValue(Border.BorderThicknessProperty, new Thickness(0.5));
                outer.SetValue(Border.MarginProperty, new Thickness(1));
                outer.AppendChild(itemsControl);

                dataGrid.Columns.Add(new DataGridTemplateColumn
                {
                    Header = week.MachineNames[i],
                    CellTemplate = new DataTemplate { VisualTree = outer },
                    Width = new DataGridLength(1, DataGridLengthUnitType.Star),
                });
            }
        }

        private static DataTemplate CreateNestRowTemplate()
        {
            FrameworkElementFactory grid = new(typeof(UniformGrid));
            grid.SetValue(UniformGrid.ColumnsProperty, 3);

            grid.AppendChild(CreateBoundCell(nameof(NestRow.NestNumber)));
            grid.AppendChild(CreateBoundCell(nameof(NestRow.OrdersComplete)));
            grid.AppendChild(CreateBoundCell(nameof(NestRow.OrdersTotal)));

            return new DataTemplate(typeof(NestRow)) { VisualTree = grid };
        }

        private static FrameworkElementFactory CreateBoundCell(string path)
        {
            FrameworkElementFactory textBlock = new(typeof(TextBlock));
            textBlock.SetBinding(TextBlock.TextProperty, new Binding(path));
            textBlock.SetValue(TextBlock.TextAlignmentProperty, TextAlignment.Center);

            FrameworkElementFactory border = new(typeof(Border));
            border.SetValue(Border.BorderBrushProperty, System.Windows.Media.Brushes.Gray);
            border.SetValue(Border.BorderThicknessProperty, new Thickness(0.5));
            border.SetValue(Border.PaddingProperty, new Thickness(4, 2, 4, 2));
            border.AppendChild(textBlock);
            return border;
        }
    }
</code></pre>
